      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part III response or note to any other line in Part III</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>STATEMENT OF PROGRAM ACCOMPLISHMENTS:The San Diego Womens Chorus performed three main concerts and two cabarets this year: our Pride Concert, with special guests Krntner Landesjugendchor, the Carinthian Youth Choir, from Austria, our fall cabaret Thank You, Next, our fall concert Hope for the Holidays, our spring cabaret Seasons of Love, and our spring concert Spark!. SDWC educated and inspired unity while entertaining and celebrating diversity, with special attention given to lesbian/LGBTQ+ and feminist perspectives. The San Diego Womens Chorus participated in a variety of community events, encouraging audiences including children and parents in more intimate settings to stand together, resist peacefully, and continue to organize for change. This year we participated in and performed at Light Up the Cathedral, the San Diego Pride Parade and Festival, the San Diego Gay Mens Chorus concert Lets Get Loud along with Coro Diversidad Tijuana, a Get Out the Vote event in partnership with local activist band The Resizters, the LGBTQ Veterans Wall of Honor Induction Ceremony at the LGBT Community Center in Hillcrest, the International Womens Day March, a local church service, Out at the Park (the Padres Pride night), Planned Parenthood of the Pacific Southwests 62nd anniversary dinner, Santee Pride, a corporate pride flag raising ceremony, Pride by the Beach in Oceanside, Poway Pride, and Carnegie Hall, where we performed a program composed entirely by women and for treble voices.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
